WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:03.170
NARUHATA

00:03.170 --> 00:05.010
NARUHATA
- Thank you very much!

00:05.010 --> 00:05.020
NARUHATA
- Whee!

00:05.020 --> 00:06.560
Whee!

00:06.560 --> 00:06.910
HATA HOUSE

00:06.910 --> 00:09.300
HATA HOUSE
- Let's hear it for the new guy!

00:09.300 --> 00:12.020
HATA HOUSE
- I think you drank a little too much.

00:12.020 --> 00:12.030
HATA HOUSE

00:12.510 --> 00:15.470
We did drink a lot again today.

00:15.470 --> 00:17.480
Want to drop in for tea somewhere?

00:18.190 --> 00:21.150
Oh, my place is near here.

00:21.150 --> 00:22.710
Would you like to stop by?

00:22.710 --> 00:25.500
I'd like to see your place, Koichi.

00:25.500 --> 00:27.190
Let's go, let's go!

00:27.190 --> 00:29.050
Time to pay a visit!

00:30.360 --> 00:31.460
Here we are.

00:38.210 --> 00:38.480
Come on, no need to be shy.

00:38.480 --> 00:40.250
- Come on, no need to be shy.
- No, I, uh...

00:40.250 --> 00:40.260
Come on, no need to be shy.

00:40.570 --> 00:43.760
I've got some yummy snacks,
and I'll make tea for everyone!

00:43.760 --> 00:46.720
Uh, hey... Wait, wait!

00:47.100 --> 00:49.360
No!

00:54.960 --> 00:58.730
Hey, there's that freshman, Haimawari.

00:59.570 --> 01:02.720
I hear he suddenly tried to take a
girl into an abandoned building.

01:02.720 --> 01:04.330
And he wouldn't take no for an answer.

01:04.330 --> 01:06.710
Oh gross. That's creepy, isn't it?

01:07.000 --> 01:10.910
What's up with that? He's more
dangerous than he looks.

01:10.910 --> 01:15.080
Yeah. They say keep your guard up with him,
no matter what gender you are.

01:15.080 --> 01:18.350
There's no telling what someone
like him does in the shadows.

01:20.430 --> 01:21.840
It's scary.

01:27.300 --> 01:31.340
My place is surprisingly spacious.

01:36.140 --> 01:37.900
Too spacious...

01:38.580 --> 01:41.420
I messed up my college debut.

01:42.550 --> 01:44.300
Hey, Gramps!

01:44.300 --> 01:47.160
I told you not to smoke in here!

01:47.160 --> 01:49.370
It's no big deal. Don't sweat it.

01:49.370 --> 01:52.250
It's shortening my lifespan!

01:52.530 --> 01:54.350
Everyone dies someday.

01:54.350 --> 01:56.090
Spare me the philosophy!

01:56.090 --> 02:00.390
I've told you, I don't want my hair
or clothes smelling like smoke!

02:00.390 --> 02:02.060
But look at me now.

02:02.510 --> 02:03.580
The party never ends in this place.

02:03.580 --> 02:05.110
- The party never ends in this place.
- Gramps!

02:05.110 --> 02:05.920
- The party never ends in this place.
- I'm always telling you, abide by
etiquette in our shared space!

02:05.920 --> 02:08.220
I'm always telling you, abide by
etiquette in our shared space!

02:09.040 --> 02:12.280
Do something, Koichi!

03:44.160 --> 03:45.240
VILLAIN

03:45.240 --> 03:50.040
VILLAIN
A CHARACTER IN A STORY OR PLAY WHO OPPOSES THE HERO;
A DELIBERATE SCOUNDREL OR CRIMINAL;
ONE BLAMED FOR A PARTICULAR EVIL OR DIFFICULTY

03:50.040 --> 03:51.160
VILLAIN
A CHARACTER IN A STORY OR PLAY WHO OPPOSES THE HERO;
A DELIBERATE SCOUNDREL OR CRIMINAL;
ONE BLAMED FOR A PARTICULAR EVIL OR DIFFICULTYJUDGMENT

03:51.160 --> 03:52.160
JUDGMENT

03:54.520 --> 03:58.460
...trying to quickly confirm their identity,
as well as investigating the cause of the fire.

03:58.460 --> 03:58.840
BABY PANDA MAKES ITS PUBLIC DEBUT
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS
FIRE AT A NARUHATA FACTORY
HEROES SAVE THE DAY ONCE MORE!

03:58.840 --> 04:00.760
BABY PANDA MAKES ITS PUBLIC DEBUT
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS
FIRE AT A NARUHATA FACTORY
HEROES SAVE THE DAY ONCE MORE!- On to our next story.

04:00.880 --> 04:00.970
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS

04:00.970 --> 04:01.220
FOLLOW-UP
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS

04:01.220 --> 04:04.240
FOLLOW-UP
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS- We have a follow-up report
on the string of jewelry store

04:04.240 --> 04:06.600
FOLLOW-UP
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS- robbery-murder incidents
that began two months ago.

04:06.600 --> 04:07.140
FOLLOW-UP
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS

04:07.140 --> 04:07.220
FOLLOW-UP
STRING OF JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY-MURDER INCIDENTS
THE SUSPECT'S IDENTITY HAS BEEN CONFIRMED

04:07.220 --> 04:10.410
THE SUSPECT'S IDENTITY HAS BEEN CONFIRMED- Police have concluded that the
suspect is Iyaro Tenba, age 27.

04:10.410 --> 04:11.230
THE SUSPECT'S IDENTITY HAS BEEN CONFIRMED- He is unemployed, has no permanent address,
and was recently released from prison.

04:11.230 --> 04:15.100
THE SUSPECT'S IDENTITY HAS BEEN CONFIRMED
UNEMPLOYED; NO PERMANENT ADDRESS
IYARO TENBA
SUSPECT (27)- He is unemployed, has no permanent address,
and was recently released from prison.

04:15.450 --> 04:17.700
The suspect, Tenba, has been
classified as a villain,

04:17.700 --> 04:22.190
and heroes have now officially
been added to the search effort.

04:31.450 --> 04:33.660
SEVERAL MONTHS LATER

04:37.750 --> 04:41.850
Today, I'll put together the
set list for my next show.

04:41.850 --> 04:44.500
And it's about time I wrote a new song.

04:50.030 --> 04:51.880
Oh, you're here, Koichi.

04:51.880 --> 04:53.430
Of course I am.

04:53.430 --> 04:55.700
Want to know why? I live here.

04:55.700 --> 04:57.860
Yes, yes, I know.

04:58.830 --> 05:01.220
Hey, you got anything to drink?

05:02.570 --> 05:03.650
CUSTARD PUDDING

05:09.210 --> 05:11.240
So, what are you up to?

05:11.510 --> 05:13.750
My hoodie got damaged, so I'm mending it.

05:13.750 --> 05:15.930
Ah, the usual one.

05:15.930 --> 05:19.060
Why not replace it with something sturdier?

05:19.060 --> 05:22.170
No. For me, it's got to be this.

05:22.510 --> 05:23.810
Done.

05:23.810 --> 05:26.880
Besides, this is official All Might merch.

05:27.250 --> 05:29.890
Just wearing it makes the
courage well up inside me!

05:30.160 --> 05:32.350
It gets you fired up, huh?

05:35.260 --> 05:38.460
I was thinking of eating that pudding.

05:39.980 --> 05:42.790
I-I never heard you say not to eat it.

05:42.790 --> 05:45.560
Write your name on it
if it's that important.

05:46.770 --> 05:48.380
It's not a big deal.

05:48.870 --> 05:52.590
You really can't back down
from a fight, can you?

05:53.440 --> 05:56.950
You have no right to talk to me like that!

05:56.950 --> 05:58.480
Sorry, sorry.

05:58.480 --> 06:01.690
Next time I buy goodies,
I'll get enough for you too.

06:01.690 --> 06:03.640
That's not what I'm talking about!

06:04.260 --> 06:07.620
And you're always so miserly.

06:07.620 --> 06:10.680
Patching up that cheap, crummy hoodie
so you can keep wearing it.

06:10.680 --> 06:12.220
It's not crummy!

06:12.220 --> 06:17.660
Say what you want about other stuff,
but I won't back down on this!

06:17.970 --> 06:20.180
Uh, yeah, you got it.

06:22.320 --> 06:24.270
They're also not cheap.

06:24.270 --> 06:27.420
They're specialty goods for hardcore fans!

06:27.420 --> 06:30.230
By the way, a limited edition
comes out each year.

06:30.230 --> 06:31.970
And I have every single one!

06:31.970 --> 06:35.820
Except the Silver Age Edition with the
established color scheme from five years ago!

06:37.150 --> 06:39.330
You're missing just the one?

06:39.670 --> 06:42.430
Oh, yeah. I ended up giving it to someone.

06:44.410 --> 06:49.160
You see, up through middle school I was
kinda serious about becoming a hero.

06:50.510 --> 06:55.640
I signed up for the entrance exam to get into
a hero course at a high school here in Tokyo.

06:55.910 --> 06:58.400
Then, on the morning of the test...

07:00.610 --> 07:03.180
Oh crap, I'm late! Oh crap, the test!

07:03.440 --> 07:05.900
Oh crap, I'm late! Oh crap, the test!

07:12.470 --> 07:13.140
Huh?

07:13.140 --> 07:14.730
Isn't the station this way?

07:15.460 --> 07:17.390
Tokyo's streets are like a maze!

07:17.390 --> 07:18.320
Oh no!

07:19.800 --> 07:21.780
A child's drowning in the river!

07:21.780 --> 07:22.990
Someone call the police!

07:22.990 --> 07:24.950
No, call the fire department!

07:24.950 --> 07:28.770
N-No, my... entrance exam...

07:34.060 --> 07:37.070
I'm...

07:39.270 --> 07:41.340
I-I am here!

07:44.710 --> 07:45.740
That's cold!

07:45.740 --> 07:47.000
And the current's quick!

07:47.000 --> 07:48.720
I'll drown!

07:52.300 --> 07:54.700
Oh. It's that shallow.

07:56.060 --> 07:58.400
You okay, sonny?

08:01.470 --> 08:03.720
F-Freezing!

08:03.720 --> 08:07.700
E-Excuse me, someone get my hoodie!

08:07.700 --> 08:09.290
Oh, you mean this! Here!

08:09.290 --> 08:11.000
No, not for me.

08:11.850 --> 08:12.950
For the kid!

08:14.140 --> 08:17.750
The test! I'm late!

08:18.790 --> 08:23.390
And then, I got there too
late to take the exam.

08:24.440 --> 08:30.760
Sometimes I wonder, would I still
be trying to become a hero

08:30.760 --> 08:32.810
if that event hadn't happened?

08:33.280 --> 08:37.990
But I figure, I left my hero spirit,
along with my prized hoodie,

08:38.580 --> 08:41.730
to that boy whose name I don't even know.

08:42.080 --> 08:42.750
WHAT MADE YOU WANT TO BE A HERO?
MAKES A BIG SPLASH!

08:42.750 --> 08:46.550
WHAT MADE YOU WANT TO BE A HERO?
MAKES A BIG SPLASH!- When I was little, somebody saved my life.

08:46.550 --> 08:48.460
WHAT MADE YOU WANT TO BE A HERO?
MAKES A BIG SPLASH!- That's what got me started down this path.

08:48.770 --> 08:53.550
Well, please offer a word for that patron
who inspired you to become a hero.

08:53.550 --> 08:53.960
Oh, he's the one from that time.

08:53.960 --> 08:55.850
- Oh, he's the one from that time.- I think you might be watching this from somewhere,
and thank you so much for what you did!

08:55.850 --> 08:56.310
I think you might be watching this from somewhere,
and thank you so much for what you did!

08:56.310 --> 08:59.170
- I think you might be watching this from somewhere,
and thank you so much for what you did!
- So, he became a hero!

08:59.690 --> 09:01.600
That'd be good enough for me.

09:02.360 --> 09:04.410
That's downright stupid.

09:04.410 --> 09:05.030
Huh?

09:05.320 --> 09:10.450
You're saying you threw away your own
future playing your usual hero games.

09:10.910 --> 09:13.700
What a dumb thing to do. I'm leaving.

09:13.700 --> 09:16.400
What are you mad about?

09:16.400 --> 09:18.950
Shouldn't you be seeing me in a new light?

09:21.380 --> 09:22.850
What just happened?

09:29.730 --> 09:30.650
Dummy.

09:31.160 --> 09:33.120
You truly are a dummy.

09:33.660 --> 09:35.620
What do you mean, "hero spirit"?

09:35.630 --> 09:36.100
HANEYAMA

09:36.100 --> 09:36.930
HANEYAMA
- What do you mean, "good enough for me"?

09:36.930 --> 09:38.090
What do you mean, "good enough for me"?

09:40.200 --> 09:42.550
Try being less of a pushover.

09:42.950 --> 09:46.110
Besides, that "boy whose
name you don't know"...

09:48.820 --> 09:51.550
That was me.

09:51.930 --> 09:54.410
And I'm not a boy!

09:56.850 --> 10:02.260
That day, as usual, I tried to use Leap
to clear the river and take a shortcut.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.840
But it rained the night before,

10:05.840 --> 10:09.330
the ground was slippery,
and the river was higher than usual.

10:13.780 --> 10:15.220
And so...

10:18.580 --> 10:23.670
He's been on my mind ever since.

10:24.080 --> 10:27.170
And even though I finally
got to meet him recently,

10:27.840 --> 10:30.440
and even though he saved me that time too,

10:31.240 --> 10:33.820
I haven't figured out a way to thank him.

10:34.210 --> 10:37.770
You really can't back down
from a fight, can you?

10:39.370 --> 10:41.250
That's not true!

10:41.570 --> 10:44.320
I can back down if I wanted!

10:49.740 --> 10:52.740
Thank you for all the times you've saved me.

10:53.260 --> 10:55.750
I'm sorry for messing
up your exam that time.

11:02.140 --> 11:07.920
I know full well you have
what it takes to be a hero.

11:08.740 --> 11:14.230
To me, you've always been a true hero!

11:18.540 --> 11:20.360
Huh? What's up?

11:20.990 --> 11:22.110
You forget something?

11:23.300 --> 11:27.120
I just... wanted to tell you something.

11:31.960 --> 11:34.340
Oh yeah? Say it, then.

11:45.780 --> 11:49.330
Pudding, huh? Isn't this stuff
women and children eat?

11:49.330 --> 11:52.200
If you don't like it,
how about you don't eat it?

11:52.200 --> 11:54.860
Um, you didn't bring any for me?

11:54.860 --> 11:56.980
He's eating your share.

11:59.150 --> 12:01.100
What'd you want to tell me, anyway?

12:01.380 --> 12:03.060
Is it about whatever's in that bag?

12:03.820 --> 12:06.770
This belongs to me! You can
keep your hands off it!

12:06.770 --> 12:07.090
- This belongs to me! You can
keep your hands off it!
- Oh, uh, sorry...

12:07.090 --> 12:08.700
- Oh, uh, sorry...
- Unbelievable!

12:09.100 --> 12:10.410
I'm leaving.

12:11.230 --> 12:13.240
Pop? Weren't you going to tell—

12:15.970 --> 12:17.430
Again?

12:17.430 --> 12:19.700
What'd she come over for?

12:20.770 --> 12:23.210
Darn it!

12:23.210 --> 12:25.950
Why do things turn out like this?!

12:32.610 --> 12:39.840
"Just wearing it makes the
courage well up inside me."

12:41.220 --> 12:42.940
Yeah, sure.

12:43.280 --> 12:45.210
Of course that doesn't happen.

12:45.930 --> 12:47.410
It's ridiculous.

13:09.430 --> 13:14.100
So, you've used up your Ideo Trigger,
and now you're out?

13:14.100 --> 13:15.220
Yeah.

13:15.880 --> 13:17.730
How do you contact your dealer?

13:18.280 --> 13:19.230
I don't.

13:19.570 --> 13:23.690
They're the one who approached
me and gave me the drug.

13:30.180 --> 13:31.690
Hi.

13:34.650 --> 13:38.210
I've got a new batch for you, Akira.

13:41.040 --> 13:42.330
A villain!

13:42.330 --> 13:43.400
Look out!

13:55.250 --> 13:57.910
I'm the guy who comes running
when there's trouble!

13:57.910 --> 13:59.730
The Crawler!

14:00.280 --> 14:02.200
Wait a minute.

14:03.770 --> 14:06.460
Didn't we already catch that villain once?

14:06.460 --> 14:07.400
The hard guy.

14:07.750 --> 14:11.330
I was sure they'd toss him
into some villain prison.

14:11.330 --> 14:13.730
Looks like you're not officially
registered as a villain

14:13.730 --> 14:16.340
unless you keep committing
Quirk-related offenses.

14:16.340 --> 14:17.580
Once isn't enough.

14:17.580 --> 14:22.410
Got it. Then we'd better stop him
before he goes on a crime spree!

14:22.410 --> 14:26.630
It always sounds like you're
sticking up for the criminal.

14:30.550 --> 14:31.880
Y-You...

14:31.880 --> 14:33.370
You again!

14:33.370 --> 14:35.720
C-Crawler!

14:40.870 --> 14:43.980
He called me "Crawler," not "Cruller!"

14:43.980 --> 14:45.940
That's nothing to be happy about!

14:46.220 --> 14:49.210
A villain calling you by name
means you're in trouble!

14:54.350 --> 14:58.080
But if he comes after me,
I can lead him to a safe place.

14:58.380 --> 15:00.290
Not that Gramps is around today.

15:00.740 --> 15:02.550
Sorry, got something to do.

15:03.780 --> 15:06.000
He does other things?

15:06.310 --> 15:08.840
You think you can catch him by yourself?

15:08.840 --> 15:10.450
Oh, no way.

15:10.450 --> 15:12.600
I'll buy some time. You call it in.

15:13.070 --> 15:15.370
Sounds about right.

15:25.220 --> 15:25.800
It's an instant villain
with a Hardening Quirk!

15:25.800 --> 15:27.700
- It's an instant villain
with a Hardening Quirk!
- You can do it, Cruller!

15:27.700 --> 15:30.080
Someone, please call the cops!

15:39.720 --> 15:40.500
Say what?

15:40.940 --> 15:43.700
This guy seems faster than last time!

15:48.050 --> 15:49.960
I think his power's increased too!

15:56.210 --> 15:59.900
What I gave to Akira is, let's see...

15:59.900 --> 16:05.520
Tr-d2c. A cocktail for
dopaminergic enhancement.

16:05.840 --> 16:08.270
So, inoculation results.

16:08.670 --> 16:10.940
I confirm a significant augmentation

16:10.940 --> 16:14.060
of both his psychological aggression
and his overall Quirk.

16:14.690 --> 16:17.930
That doesn't carry much impact, does it?

16:17.930 --> 16:21.360
I wish I could see firsthand
how solid the guy is.

16:21.360 --> 16:23.040
Oh hey, it's Hachisuka.

16:23.040 --> 16:25.460
What're you doing? Homework?

16:26.960 --> 16:29.270
It's a report for my job.

16:30.060 --> 16:31.470
Sounds like a pain.

16:31.470 --> 16:34.540
The pay makes it worth it.

16:39.640 --> 16:40.790
I'm in trouble.

16:40.790 --> 16:42.730
The ground's all cratered from his punches.

16:42.730 --> 16:44.430
It's gotten hard to move around!

16:45.680 --> 16:46.740
Crap!

16:51.950 --> 16:52.940
Koichi!

17:02.470 --> 17:05.120
Ah, a new development.

17:20.190 --> 17:21.500
You're a hard one.

17:30.170 --> 17:31.860
Here come the police!

17:36.340 --> 17:37.490
He ran off!

17:38.560 --> 17:40.650
We've got to get away too!

17:44.590 --> 17:47.470
Uh, thanks for saving me.

17:47.880 --> 17:49.410
Who are you?

17:50.760 --> 17:54.810
I'm Stendhal. A meddler, like yourself.

17:57.070 --> 17:58.260
We'll meet again.

18:07.350 --> 18:10.430
I can't believe how cool that guy was!

18:10.990 --> 18:13.400
Overpowering villains with a sword!

18:13.400 --> 18:16.620
Maybe I'll carry one around too!

18:16.620 --> 18:18.560
You let people influence you too much.

18:20.760 --> 18:23.650
I just got a message from Samazu and crew.

18:24.050 --> 18:25.670
Let's see.

18:26.090 --> 18:27.950
The "Legendary Alum"?

18:27.950 --> 18:28.450
Mhm.

18:28.540 --> 18:28.790
NARUHATA

18:28.790 --> 18:34.390
NARUHATA
- He said there's this famous kick-ass
fighter who used to go to his school.

18:34.390 --> 18:34.810
NARUHATA

18:34.810 --> 18:37.980
NARUHATA
- He's all manly and can't
abide any wrongdoing.

18:37.980 --> 18:40.930
NARUHATA
- I just transferred here,
so I'm not in the know.

18:41.300 --> 18:45.420
So, when they told him about us,
he said he wants to meet us.

18:45.420 --> 18:47.520
At the restaurant in front of the station.

18:47.520 --> 18:51.890
Sounds good. I'd love to
work more with the locals!

18:52.230 --> 18:55.650
I tell you, it's just
like with Mr. Stendhal.

18:55.650 --> 18:59.480
This place has plenty of people
with a strong sense of justice!

18:59.480 --> 19:04.410
I hope these hidden-hero types
become more and more active.

19:04.770 --> 19:06.480
I'll do my part too.

19:06.480 --> 19:07.950
Yeah, but...

19:07.950 --> 19:13.020
People who get into fights based on their
own sense of justice are dangerous.

19:13.020 --> 19:14.540
That's common sense.

19:14.990 --> 19:16.020
Huh?

19:16.020 --> 19:17.630
What's wrong?

19:17.630 --> 19:20.230
No, I mean, that's...

19:20.700 --> 19:22.790
Huh? Common sense?

19:22.790 --> 19:26.800
Dangerous people... You
might have a point.

19:26.800 --> 19:30.850
I told you, you shouldn't take
what this guy says seriously!

19:30.850 --> 19:35.220
The alum guy is coming to meet me
and Koichi, so you keep out of it!

19:39.720 --> 19:42.790
Hey. The geezer's not with you today?

19:48.620 --> 19:51.030
You know him already?

19:51.030 --> 19:54.690
Th-That's one way of putting it.

19:54.690 --> 19:55.840
Doesn't even come close!

19:57.070 --> 19:59.810
What the hell do you guys think I am?

20:00.160 --> 20:02.250
"What," you ask?

20:02.720 --> 20:06.840
I mean, it's like...
What's the right way to put it?

20:06.840 --> 20:08.760
You're the Dox 'n' Murder Man!

20:08.760 --> 20:10.590
Yeah, that's it.

20:11.110 --> 20:12.470
Forget this.

20:12.910 --> 20:15.100
It'd be a waste of time talking to just you two.

20:18.800 --> 20:19.900
Sir...

20:21.040 --> 20:22.750
What did he want to discuss?

20:22.750 --> 20:24.740
Who cares?! He's not worth it!

20:53.320 --> 20:56.060
Looks like your eyes aren't hardened.

20:57.260 --> 21:00.150
And when your focus wanders
due to pain and fear,

21:00.150 --> 21:02.830
the rest of your Hardening weakens as well.

21:03.270 --> 21:06.290
Do you know why you're scared and in pain?

21:07.130 --> 21:10.570
It's because you lack conviction.

21:12.110 --> 21:16.370
When you wield power without conviction,
that's called crime.

21:16.810 --> 21:20.650
When crime takes the shape of a person,
they're called a villain.

21:21.340 --> 21:25.800
With a single sword stroke,
I eliminate the crime you embody.

21:30.720 --> 21:32.220
In other words...

21:34.220 --> 21:35.450
judgment.

21:39.580 --> 21:40.570
Now then...

21:41.760 --> 21:44.270
Next, this guy.

21:53.350 --> 21:54.630
Nice.

23:26.040 --> 23:30.220
Societal rules are there so we
can all have peace of mind.

23:30.220 --> 23:33.150
But as a vigilante, I operate
outside those rules.

23:33.460 --> 23:35.020
Next time, "Crossing Lines."

23:35.257 --> 23:39.265
I want to do what I think is right,
not what's good or bad.
